<title>JAPAN: Japan gives securities licences to two bank units.</title>
<headline>Japan gives securities licences to two bank units.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance said on Tuesday that it had given licences to conduct securities brokering to Shinkin Securities Co Ltd and BOY Securities Co Ltd, both subsidiaries of Japanese banks.</p>
<p>Shinkin Securities is the securities unit of Zenshinren Bank, a national association of credit associations, and BOY Securities is fully owned by the Bank of Yokohama Ltd.</p>
